# Accepted findings for this example image.
#
# TEE-Crafter's vulnerability gate blocks on findings that have an upstream fix
# (apps/cli/src/tee_crafter/core/security/vuln_scan.py; the thresholds are in
# cli/commands/deploy/flow_container.py — fixable CRITICAL must be 0 and
# fixable HIGH must be 0).  The two below are reported as fixable but cannot be
# fixed in this image.  Each was traced to ground in the built image before
# being listed here; do not add entries without doing the same.
#
# Both come from `site-packages/pip/_vendor/vendor.txt`, the pinned manifest of
# pip's *own* vendored tree — not from anything this app or the PyTorch base
# image installs.  Read out of `gpu-cc-example:fixed` on 2026-08-22:
#
#   $ grep -iE '^(msgpack|setuptools)' \
#       /opt/conda/lib/python3.11/site-packages/pip/_vendor/vendor.txt
#   msgpack==1.1.2
#   setuptools==70.3.0
#
#   $ python -c "import importlib.metadata as m; print(m.version('setuptools'))"
#   84.0.0
#   $ python -c "import importlib.metadata as m; m.version('msgpack')"
#   PackageNotFoundError
#
# So setuptools is installed at 84.0.0 — well past the 78.1.1 the finding asks
# for — and msgpack is not installed at all.  Upgrading cannot clear either.
#
# There is no upstream fix to wait for: this image carries pip 26.2.1, the
# current release, and it still vendors exactly these two versions.
#
# And pip cannot be removed.  TEE-Crafter's generated container Dockerfile does
# `FROM __USER_IMAGE__` followed by `RUN python -m pip install`
# (templates/common/Dockerfile.container.template) to layer the TEE runtime on
# top, so stripping pip here breaks every deploy of this example.  The same
# conclusion was reached the hard way in examples/hello_http.
#
# Re-check on a pip release that refreshes its vendored msgpack/setuptools, and
# delete the corresponding line when it does.
#
# Deliberately NOT listed, so that they stay visible in the report:
#   * CVE-2026-59890 — setuptools MEDIUM, same vendored 70.3.0 entry as
#     CVE-2025-47273 below.  MEDIUM findings are gated at 25, and this image has
#     3, so it does not block and does not need accepting.
#   * CVE-2025-2999 / CVE-2025-3730 — torch MEDIUMs, fixed in 2.9.1 and 2.8.0.
#     Genuinely fixable by moving the base image forward again; kept in the
#     report because that is a real (if unforced) upgrade, not an accepted risk.
#     See the Dockerfile for why the base sits at 2.6.0.

# setuptools: path traversal in PackageIndex. pip-vendored manifest entry only.
CVE-2025-47273

# msgpack: OOB read on Unpacker reuse. pip-vendored manifest entry only.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
